# Test-Driven Development

When writing code, including bugfixes, work test-first:

1. Create focused tests for the intended behavior before implementation.
2. Run the tests and verify they fail in the expected way.
3. Implement the smallest change that satisfies the tests.
4. Run the tests again and verify they pass.

Treat tests as being just as important as the implementation. Take the same
care to document why each test exists and exactly what behavior it verifies.

Skip this only when tests are clearly not viable, and state why.
